It seems the RNG took pity on me after so many failed vegetarian
Tourist attempts, and, for the second game in a row, granted me an
early wand of wishing. That plus several magic lamps and plentiful
altars finally made sweet victory within reach.

I wasted a *lot* of time in this game, unfortunately. I was very
inefficient in buying protection - there were no temples generated
other than those guaranteed in the game, and I didn't get teleport
control until very late, necessitating a lot of walking around
gathering gold and then getting back to the Minetown priest. Then I
stupidly tried on an un-IDd helm from a polypile, which turned out to
be opposite alignment, and lost all my protection. Thus forcing me to
gather all the gold from Ludios (nearly getting killed by Croesus in
the process, having a relatively poor AC at the time), stuffing it
into the bag of holding fortunately granted by Sokoban, and buying the
protection back in Minetown. I then evilly commanded my pet winged
gargoyle to kill the priest for his robe and spellbooks.

I spent a lot of time polypiling and a bit pudding farming, neither of
which was terribly productive. Though altar camping did grant me
pretty much every neutral weapon in the game, it took a long time to
get my favorites, Frost Brand and Magicbane. I two-weaponed these (FB
until getting the Book, then mostly MB to avoid curses) with a silver
saber.

I was very conservative with my wishes despite having so many, and
after the starting amulet of reflection, gray dragon scale, ring of
slow digestion, and magic marker, waited for quite awhile before
finally wishing up a helm of brilliance and ring of teleport control.
I found two more such rings in Gehennom, prompting me to polymorph
into a xorn and eat them (I rarely polyself, but wanted to save ring
space for slow digestion and conflict). Luckily, the second steel ring
spread magic throughout my body.

I was glad I opted for GDSM + robe + AoR as I learned and cast a lot
of spells. Charm monster was more fun than necessary, as I've
developed a fondness for winged gargoyles (fast, flying, don't eat,
stoning-resistant) and tamed several throughout the game.
Unfortunately my last died on the Plane of Fire; they're not
particularly fireproof. Magic mapping turned out to be the most useful
spell, as after wasting so much time in the main dungeon, I wanted to
get through Gehennom as fast as possible.

I bribed Asmodeus and Baalzebub (again to save time), killed Juiblex
before he even swallowed me, and dispatched Orcus before he completely
emptied his wand of death. The trip back up was uneventful; having
PYEC to recharge the death wand made it trivial to kill Rodney. Took
awhile to find the portal on the Plane of Fire, as usual, but at least
no archons showed up. Killed off Death and Famine easily enough,
avoided Pestilence, and after visiting two of the high altars, offered
the Amulet for my fourth NAO victory and second consecutive ascension.
